\newlabel{tab:grid}{{2}{4}{}{table.2}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Architecture of the study. Prompts from four task families (1) run through the eight-cell grid under metered board power and are graded (2). The grades and costs form a label table, from which routers learn the probability that each cell succeeds and a threshold $\tau $ selects a cell (3). Manual and routed policies are then charged by one cost function, the router's own cost included, and yield the escalation tax and its companions (4). The public and hosted pools reuse the policy and tax code without local inference (5).}}{5}{}\protected@file@percent }
